{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Challenges to Cloud Computing"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when talking about cloud services concerns. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Interpret the IT needs assessment, to determine the required technology to manage information, according to the rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Supposed To in Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To ask about things that are expected to happen, you must use <strong>be</strong> <strong>supposed to in interrogative form</strong>.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Is cloud computing supposed to be cheaper in the long run?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Be supposed</strong> to in questions is used to ask about something somebody should do or has to do. It is also used when you want to ask about something you are expecting to happen.</p> <p>The grammatical structure that needs to be followed is:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Verb Be+ Subject + Supposed to + Verb + Complement + ?</strong></p> <p>Example:</p> <p><strong><i>Are you supposed to get</i></strong><i> the cloud services for your company?</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are cloud computing services supposed to be more secure at least?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are you, providers, supposed to upgrade and advance the product?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Understanding technological edge or cutting edge technology"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<div align=\"justify\">Cutting-edge technology is about the technological devices, techniques, or achievements that use the most updated and high-level information technology developments."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div align=\"justify\">Technological edge is the process of leading and promoting IT industry organizations. Cutting-edge technology refers to developing technology features, different to bleeding-edge technology that does not offer reliability to users.<br/><br/>  This term is applied to any type of technology, especially in the context of marketing. It refers to the most sophisticated developments in technology. It is basically used to describe the best technological inventions; not necessarily the newest though."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "challenge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that needs to be explained or justified"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am here to report some issues and challenges I've got with the cloud services."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "concern"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a problem or something that is causing worry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "examp